From b6bab6e18dfab04a4d145b5a199c0398b2ffc615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 02:50:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 2/4 remainder: LinkArea, scroll props, up-down accel,
 IMessageFilter

Additive controls-support types (signatures from the net48 reference):

- LinkArea struct (Start/Length/IsEmpty/equality) for LinkLabel.
- ScrollProperties + HScrollProperties/VScrollProperties, now exposed as
  ScrollableControl.HorizontalScroll/VerticalScroll (previously commented out).
- NumericUpDownAcceleration + NumericUpDownAccelerationCollection (sorted by
  Seconds), exposed as NumericUpDown.Accelerations.
- ToolStripItemEventArgs, ToolStripDropDownClosedEventArgs,
  ToolStripDropDownClosingEventArgs (+ their delegate handlers).
- IMessageFilter + Application.AddMessageFilter/RemoveMessageFilter/FilterMessage.
  GTK has no Win32 pump, so filters are stored and run on demand via FilterMessage
  rather than by an internal pump - a documented boundary.

Net48 public types present 622->635 (missing 412->399, under 400). Full suite
green at 2326 (+6 tests covering LinkArea value semantics, scroll defaults,
acceleration validation + sorted collection, ToolStrip event args, and the
Application message-filter add/filter/remove cycle).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
